From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Exercise Linux watchdogs without an ICMP socket

The watchdog tests need a process that survives until the timeout. On a
Linux build worker without ICMP socket access, ping exits before the
watchdog fires. Keep the shell child in the script case and use a process
that writes to its pipe before waiting in the direct command case.

Upstream: pending
Reference: https://github.com/apache/commons-exec/blob/4a27212367272c91da8dc01732f9c20be964de48/src/test/java/org/apache/commons/exec/issues/Exec41Test.java
---
--- a/src/test/scripts/ping.sh
+++ b/src/test/scripts/ping.sh
@@ -21,7 +21,10 @@
 
 echo "[ping.sh] Blocking for $1 seconds ..."
 # see EXEC-52 - option must appear after the hostname!
-if test "$(uname -s)" = "HP-UX"
+if test "$(uname -s)" = "Linux"
+then
+        sleep "$1"
+elif test "$(uname -s)" = "HP-UX"
 then
         ping 127.0.0.1 -n $1
 else
--- a/src/test/java/org/apache/commons/exec/issues/Exec41Test.java
+++ b/src/test/java/org/apache/commons/exec/issues/Exec41Test.java
@@ -99,6 +99,9 @@
 
         if (OS.isFamilyWindows()) {
             cmdLine = CommandLine.parse("ping.exe -n 10 -w 1000 127.0.0.1");
+        } else if ("Linux".equals(SystemProperties.getOsName())) {
+            // Exercise the pipe and watchdog without requiring ICMP socket permissions.
+            cmdLine = new CommandLine("sh").addArgument("-c").addArgument("echo watchdog; exec sleep 10", false);
         } else if ("HP-UX".equals(SystemProperties.getOsName())) {
             // see EXEC-52 - option must appear after the hostname!
             cmdLine = CommandLine.parse("ping 127.0.0.1 -n 10");
